{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145626",
      "title": "How NextJS Prepares & Pre-renders Pages",
      "lectureOrder": 265,
      "videoOrder": 246,
      "sourceHash": "b6932b558e2c4954c6b0a874748df104fc703d376b0e08df05d9ea552ae23e5f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 5.98,
          "en": "So, I outlined a potential problem we could be facing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.98,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "in the last lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 12.293,
          "en": "Now Next.js can help us with a concept called pre-rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.16,
          "end": 15.88,
          "en": "Imagine that you have some page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.88,
          "end": 18.76,
          "en": "some route which then loads some page file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.76,
          "end": 21.74,
          "en": "in the pages folder, which needs data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.74,
          "end": 25.09,
          "en": "Now when a request is sent to this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.09,
          "end": 28.07,
          "en": "so if a user wants to visit this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.07,
          "end": 30.67,
          "en": "then what Next.js does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.67,
          "end": 35.49,
          "en": "is it will return a pre-rendered page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.49,
          "end": 38.56,
          "en": "And that's a difference to standard React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.56,
          "end": 43.42,
          "en": "With standard React, you get back an empty HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.42,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "and all the JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 48.52,
          "en": "And then that JavaScript code runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.52,
          "end": 50.86,
          "en": "and brings something onto the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.86,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "And that happens super fast",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "so users won't really see a problem there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 58.34,
          "en": "But then any data which might be needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.34,
          "end": 61.52,
          "en": "in addition to the general DOM structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.52,
          "end": 62.66,
          "en": "that should be showed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.66,
          "end": 65.49,
          "en": "such data then is loaded from a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.49,
          "end": 67.66,
          "en": "and that can take a while.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.66,
          "end": 70.3,
          "en": "Now not if the page is pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.3,
          "end": 73.53999999999999,
          "en": "And that is what Next.js does for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.53999999999999,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "Instead of loading data only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "after the page was sent back to the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 82.75,
          "en": "Next.js pre-renders a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.75,
          "end": 86.28999999999999,
          "en": "and pre-renders all the HTML content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.28999999999999,
          "end": 88.76,
          "en": "with all the data that might be needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.76,
          "end": 90.92,
          "en": "It loads that in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.92,
          "end": 95.02000000000001,
          "en": "and then pre-generates the finished HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.02000000000001,
          "end": 99.91,
          "en": "so that it's this finished, fully populated HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.91,
          "end": 104.27000000000001,
          "en": "which can be sent back to the client, so to the visitor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.27000000000001,
          "end": 107.18,
          "en": "So that's great for SEO.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.18,
          "end": 109.33,
          "en": "Now we also of course still want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.33,
          "end": 111.75999999999999,
          "en": "to have an interactive React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.75999999999999,
          "end": 114.14,
          "en": "After all, there is a reason why we use React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.14,
          "end": 118.28999999999999,
          "en": "and we don't just build a HTML and CSS app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 120.15,
          "en": "Instead, we might be using React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.15,
          "end": 122.32,
          "en": "for handling user interaction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.32,
          "end": 125.42,
          "en": "for watching a forum and showing validation errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.42,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "for reacting to button clicks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 129.59,
          "en": "And therefore Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.59,
          "end": 133.34,
          "en": "will not just send back this pre-rendered page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.34,
          "end": 136.37,
          "en": "but it will also send back all the JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.37,
          "end": 138.05,
          "en": "that belongs to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.05,
          "end": 139.37,
          "en": "And it will do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.37,
          "end": 142.48,
          "en": "which is called hydrating that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.48,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "So it will send back that JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 149.77,
          "en": "and that code will then take over that pre-rendered page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.77,
          "end": 152.82999999999998,
          "en": "and again let React do its job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.82999999999998,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "That is great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 157.13,
          "en": "because now we have an interactive page or app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.13,
          "end": 160.48,
          "en": "But we did send back that pre-rendered page initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.48,
          "end": 163.41,
          "en": "so that all the core content was already there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.41,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "right from the start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 168.7,
          "en": "and so that search engine crawlers, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.7,
          "end": 172.86,
          "en": "also see that entire page with all the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.86,
          "end": 175.09,
          "en": "If it's not interactive at that point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.09,
          "end": 177.45,
          "en": "that doesn't matter to those crawlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.45,
          "end": 181.213,
          "en": "because they are only interested in the content anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.07,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "So that's the idea of pre-rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 189.95,
          "en": "We, or to be precise, Next.js, prepare a page in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.12,
          "end": 194.54,
          "en": "by pre-building all the HTML content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.54,
          "end": 197.05,
          "en": "and by pre-loading all the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.05,
          "end": 198.98,
          "en": "that will eventually be needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.98,
          "end": 202.88,
          "en": "And it is worth pointing out that this pre-rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.88,
          "end": 206.26,
          "en": "only affects the initial load.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.26,
          "end": 210.8,
          "en": "So when we visit a page and we load our first page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.8,
          "end": 213.07999999999998,
          "en": "this page is pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.07999999999998,
          "end": 215.28,
          "en": "Once we are on a website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.28,
          "end": 218.12,
          "en": "that's powered by Next.js and React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.12,
          "end": 220.39,
          "en": "and once that page is hydrated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.39,
          "end": 223.94,
          "en": "which happens right after this first rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.94,
          "end": 225.32999999999998,
          "en": "once that is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.32999999999998,
          "end": 229.28,
          "en": "we have a standard single page application again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 229.28,
          "end": 231.25,
          "en": "So then React takes over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.25,
          "end": 233.53,
          "en": "and handles everything on the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.53,
          "end": 235.54,
          "en": "If the page changes thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.54,
          "end": 239.47,
          "en": "if we visit a different page of that same website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.47,
          "end": 241.86,
          "en": "that page is not pre-rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.86,
          "end": 245.7,
          "en": "but instead created in the client with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.7,
          "end": 249,
          "en": "It's just this initial page which we visit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 249,
          "end": 250.39,
          "en": "which is pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.39,
          "end": 253.28,
          "en": "So that there we don't get this empty page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.28,
          "end": 255.03,
          "en": "until React is ready,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 255.03,
          "end": 257.33,
          "en": "but we get this pre-rendered page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.33,
          "end": 260.673,
          "en": "which contains all that initial content already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.58,
          "end": 263.18,
          "en": "And for achieving this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 263.18,
          "end": 266.95,
          "en": "Next.js has two forms of pre-rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.95,
          "end": 270.15,
          "en": "and we are, of course, going to learn about both,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.15,
          "end": 271.78,
          "en": "which you can choose from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.78,
          "end": 274.76,
          "en": "So you can choose which form you wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.76,
          "end": 277.97,
          "en": "The first form, and the recommended form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.97,
          "end": 280.81,
          "en": "is static generation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 280.81,
          "end": 285.81,
          "en": "The other form, the alternative, is server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.03,
          "end": 288.76,
          "en": "Now that might not tell you much right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 288.76,
          "end": 291.95,
          "en": "I will explain both throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.95,
          "end": 295.56,
          "en": "The main difference is that with static generation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 295.56,
          "end": 298.2,
          "en": "all the pages are pre-generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.2,
          "end": 300.88,
          "en": "in advance during build time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 300.88,
          "end": 304.18,
          "en": "So when you build your application for production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 304.18,
          "end": 308.62,
          "en": "before you deploy it, you prepare all those pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 308.62,
          "end": 313.62,
          "en": "With server-side rendering, pages are created just in time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 313.67,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "after deployment when a request reaches the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 320.05,
          "en": "Now there are also ways of mixing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 320.05,
          "end": 323.07,
          "en": "and I will dive deeply into both concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 323.07,
          "end": 326.123,
          "en": "and when to use which throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327,
          "end": 329.05,
          "en": "I hope it's clear what the core idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 329.05,
          "end": 330.83,
          "en": "behind pre-rendering is, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 330.83,
          "end": 334.2,
          "en": "and therefore, let's now explore these different concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 336.183,
          "en": "of pre-rendering pages.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
